    "summary": "Panel; carved from wood. Rectangular in form, part openwork; front surface carved in low relief with central figure of Oba with mudfish legs, arms supported on both sides by attendants. Naked male figure holding ada sword at right side. Umbrella and right arm depicted on left side. Border at top and bottom has alternating carvings of frogs and shells. Bottom border has inscription in centre. Side borders carved with frogs, shells and human arms. Two metal picture hooks at top.",
